# state: any   (golden 77a5f0908dce promoted 2026-10-11; lane.savestate433)
# Grand Theft Auto: Vice City (5454000F): one route, first-run or on the
# golden. PATHFOUND by pathfind.py on the Nova, 2026-10-11
# (lane.gtaroutes1011 session 1056194; path recorded to
# pathknow/paths/5454000F.json, gameplay reached in 1.5 min / 9 steps).
#
# NOT what the brief expected: there is no "Start Game" / "New Game" menu
# and no title-screen START press on this disk's first run. The two
# Rockstar publisher-logo screens (A skips each) lead straight into the
# "In the Beginning..." cutscene (three segments, A skips each), then
# Tommy on foot at the Ocean View Hotel, full HUD (health, money, radar,
# wanted level). Recorded twice by the pathfind session (gameplay and a
# follow-up probe); no menu state was ever seen.
#
# The logo and cutscene skips are trains of A presses 5 s apart (as
# gta-sa.route): loading time differs between runs, and an A that lands on
# a loading screen is a no-op. The play pattern runs, sprints, steers and
# turns the camera; it never presses Y, START or BACK.
#
wait 40
press A 300
wait 5
press A 300
wait 5
press A 300
wait 5
press A 300
wait 5
shot logoskip
wait 10
shot loading
press A 300
wait 5
press A 300
wait 5
press A 300
wait 5
press A 300
wait 5
press A 300
wait 5
press A 300
wait 5
shot cutscenes
wait 5
mark gameplay
repeat forever {
    repeat 4 {
        axis LY min
        press A 200
        wait 1.5
        axis LX max
        wait 1
        axis LX mid
        press A 200
        wait 1.5
        axis LX min
        wait 1
        axis LX mid
        axis RX max
        wait 0.5
        axis RX mid
        wait 1
        axis LY mid
        wait 0.5
    }
    # wedge escape (gtawedge1012): the loop above only drifts heading right
    # 0.5s of RX max per ~10s cycle, which does not turn far enough to clear
    # a recess once Tommy is run face-first into one (confirmation
    # 1-1791785130-lane.local-2108844 wedged in a garage-door alcove at
    # 23:41:54 and never moved again for the rest of the run). Back off
    # first -- LY max is camera-relative, so it runs him toward the camera
    # and away from whatever he is pressed against -- then swing the camera
    # hard before the next run-forward leg picks a new heading.
    axis LY max
    wait 2
    axis RX max
    wait 1.5
    axis LX mid
    axis LY mid
    axis RX mid
}
